# DEV environment — part of the engine's own core framework config, alongside .env,
# framework.yaml, and locators/. Unlike engine/.env (git-ignored, holds local secrets),
# this file IS committed: for a test framework, the target URLs themselves usually
# aren't secret, only credentials are (those still live in engine/.env / CI secrets).
#
# Read only by the backend's EnvironmentConfigService (Path: <engine dir>/.env.<name>,
# lowercase) when a run targets environment "DEV" — the engine process itself never
# reads this file directly. Fill in real values below; until BASE_URL and API_BASE_URL
# are both set, triggering a run against DEV fails fast with a clear error.

BASE_URL=https://demowebshop.tricentis.com/
API_BASE_URL=https://demowebshop.tricentis.com/
